    "content": "\"Read option V3 \\\"Motif calls emitted for Capsida NR001–NR005 and Lir Starfish binding-assay readouts\\\" in the option record below. I'm thinking about running something on this with up to $1,000 of GPU credit at Lambda's on-demand prices (https://lambda.ai/pricing). Make it concrete: what to build, the baseline, how to check it's right, and the cost. Cite a URL for every factual claim. Write to /home/hal/dev/interp/metis/experiments/blind-01/20261021-0116-loop/out/r1/card/work/seed-1/seed/idea/95fa97ae/producer.md. Option record: {\\\"id\\\":\\\"V3\\\",\\\"title\\\":\\\"Motif calls emitted for Capsida NR001–NR005 and Lir Starfish binding-assay readouts\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"Enumerate binding modes of capsid libraries against the human BBB-receptor set used by Capsida's NR001–NR005 platform and Lir's Starfish capsid-structure pipeline (ALPL, AAVR, LRP6 and their panel partners) with docking, MD refinement and AlphaFold-Multimer, emitting calls in the format of plate- and bead-based capsid–receptor binding assays. Score whether 3-fold-axis engagement geometry agrees with measured bind/no-bind receptor by receptor, then rank the binding-positive pairs as the only candidates worth a transcytosis claim. Published modeling covers only single-digit complexes, and neither Capsida's nor Lir's structural pipeline has been assessed against exhaustive enumeration. Narrowing: Leaves aside transcytosis and all post-binding fate — the observable is binding agreement plus interface geometry, not fate. It still moves the root question by narrowing the candidate signature catalog (Q3) to pairs that survive a human-receptor binding assay, which is the precondition for any sufficiency test (Q1).\\\",\\\"root_link\\\":\\\"Bears on Q3 of the root question — which capsid–receptor binding signatures are candidates for transcytosis — by pruning the catalog to pairs that survive a real human-receptor binding assay before any transcytosis claim (Q1) is attempted.\\\",\\\"compute_open\\\":\\\"More parallel compute buys model runs across capsid × receptor × pose for the NR001–NR005 receptor set, letting the shared-motif question be tested receptor by receptor against binding readouts rather than at a single receptor; published depth effects stop at single-digit complexes and the proprietary pipelines are unmeasured, so the payoff is unknown.\\\",\\\"sequential\\\":\\\"none: each capsid–receptor pose is an independent docking or AlphaFold-Multimer job with its own seeds, and the plate/bead binding readouts are a separate block.\\\",\\\"source_urls\\\":[]}. Root question: Can molecular mapping of AAV capsid-receptor interactions on brain microvascular endothelial cells determine which AAV variants transcytose across the blood-brain barrier versus remain intracellular, and for which capsid-receptor binding signatures?. Read only pages you fetch and what you write under /home/hal/dev/interp/metis/experiments/blind-01/20261021-0116-loop/out/r1/card/work/seed-1/seed/idea/95fa97ae; write only under /home/hal/dev/interp/metis/experiments/blind-01/20261021-0116-loop/out/r1/card/work/seed-1/seed/idea/95fa97ae. When the plan is written, return it as the record in your output schema; producer.md stays your working file. In the record, put every number the cost or the size of the test depends on in numbers, each with a basis: CITED (a page states this number for this same setting; give the page text that shows it), PROXY (a page states it for a different model, GPU, dataset, size or component; give the page text and say what differs), MEASURED (you ran code: save the script and its output under /home/hal/dev/interp/metis/experiments/blind-01/20261021-0116-loop/out/r1/card/work/seed-1/seed/idea/95fa97ae/pilot/ and give the output line and the machine), DERIVED (an expression over other ids), DESIGN (your choice), or GUESS (no source; say what it rests on). Give each rate as the per-GPU price and the GPU count, and each line's hours as an expression. A line's hours are wall-clock hours of the whole instance, not GPU-hours: 40 GPU-hours on an 8-GPU instance are 5 hours. The default line is a time box: DESIGN hours at a rate from the prices below, ended by a timer or stop rule; it needs no estimate of the work inside it, but if you have one, put it in need. Use GUESS only where a number drives the plan. For each PROXY or GUESS the cost or result depends on, name the phase that measures it in measured_by, and give that phase's threshold as gate if your plan changes on it. Optional: scenarios (pessimistic or sensitivity cases, as values for the inputs they change), optional lines for stretch work, instead_of for fallbacks, and yields (the number ids that say what the money buys: cases, samples, primes). Refer to the budget as budget_usd and to the price sheet's filesystem price as fs_usd_gib_month. List human time and money outside Lambda in outside_budget. predictions.if_lever and predictions.if_not are the outcomes you expect, on the same measured quantity, if more compute does or does not change the answer. predictions.noise_rule says how you will tell a real difference from run-to-run noise. predictions.expected is the outcome you expect, if_lever, if_not or unsure, with one sentence why. scored_against says what the measured outcome is compared with to decide it is correct. Each source carries the exact sentence from the page that you rely on. Cite pages a reader can open without a login or paywall: a value that appears only in a paywalled full text cannot be checked, so take it from an open source (an open-access version, a preprint or a public database). In restructuring, sequential_part is the part of this computation that one answer waits on step after step, and how many steps; method is why those steps need not run in order and how your plan computes them at the same time instead, or \\\"none\\\" if the plan only runs independent work side by side or splits each step across GPUs. If method is not none,