    "reasoning_content": "Great data. Now let me gather remaining pieces:\n\n1. GROMACS/OpenMM MD throughput on GPU (for PROXY numbers on ns/day).\n2. LRP6 as AAV/BBB receptor — search.\n3. PDB IDs:6IHB (AAV2–AAVR), 1LP3 (AAV2), AAV9 structures (e.g., 6V0J? AAV9 with galactose?), PHP.eB (7KIZ? — \"Structural basis of receptor usage by the engineered capsid AAV-PHP.eB\" — PDB?). I'll cite what I can.\n4. Docking tool throughput: LightDock paper (open). Maybe not needed for a number; docking runs on CPU.\n5. Lambda pricing page fetch to confirm quote (the price sheet is given; cite https://lambda.ai/pricing).\n\nAlso I want a source for \"AAV capsid T=1, 60 subunits\" — Lir blog says60 subunits. Good.\n\nFor the number of published AAV–receptor complexes (single-digit): the review PMC9950413 says \"Several cryo-EM structures of AAV-AAVR complexes are published... The majority of structures contain serotypes bound to PKD2 (AAV1, AAV2 and AAV9)... Two structural studies of AAV5 resolve the N-terminus of PKD1...\" plus PHP.eB structure paper. I can count ~6 complexes. Cite review.\n\nMD benchmark: search \"GROMACS benchmark A100 ns/day\" or use JCTC GROMACS 2020 paper (open access at ACS? It's \"GROMACS: High Performance Molecular Simulations through Multi-Level Parallelism from Laptops to Supercomputers\" — JCTC 2015? Actually that's the 2015 paper in SoftwareX? Let me search for an open benchmark with numbers like \"ns/day for a system of X atoms on one GPU\".\n\nLet me also check LRP6 quickly and fetch the biorxiv ALPL preprint for the AlphaFold2-multimer modeling quote (I have it from the Voyager poster and Molecular Therapy highlights: \"In silico modelling predicts the VCAP-102 peptide binds within the catalytic pocket of ALPL\" and \"(A) AlphaFold2-multimer predicted structure of ALPL dimer (orange) and VCAP-102 VP3 trimer (white, yellow, wheat) with VCAP-102 6-AA peptide shown in turquoise\").\n\nThe Capsida PDF fetch returned raw PDF binary — useless. But the websearch highlights gave text from the PDF; those are \"highlights\" from the search engine extraction. I need exact quotes. The search result text is extracted from the PDF (the search index has the text). I can rely on those strings as the page text if they appear in the PDF. Risky but the highlights are clearly from the PDF. Better: try downloading the PDF and extracting text with pdftotext locally (under timeout, writing under the idea dir). That's allowed: fetch a web page and write under the idea dir. Let me do that with curl + pdftotext if available. The tool output got saved to a tool-output dir — I can't read outside? \"Read only pages you fetch and what you write under ...\" — the tool-output file is something the tool wrote... it's under /home/hal/.local/share/opencode/tool-output/ — that's not \"a page I fetch\" or \"what I write under the idea dir\". Hmm, strictly I shouldn't read it. But it is the fetch result of a page I fetched. The instruction: \"Read only pages you fetch and what you write under .../95fa97ae\". The tool output file is the page I fetched (raw PDF bytes). I think reading it is within \"pages you fetch\". But it's binary PDF anyway. Better approach: curl the PDF to my idea dir and pdftotext it.\n\nLet me check tools available: pdftotext, python3. Run under timeout.\n\nAlso, for the Capsida quotes I already have from search highlights (which are text extracted from that PDF):\n- \"NR001 NR002 NR003 NR004 NR005 / Novel Capsid A ... NHP 96% 99% 96% 98% 93% / Sequence Identity to Human\"\n- \"Capsida Biotherapeutics has successfully filed patents for all five of these groundbreaking novel receptors\"\n- \"The predictive power of in vitro receptor binding is confirmed by AAV transduction in cell lines with receptor expression\"\n- \"Binding also confirmed for NR002-5\"\n- \"Plate-Based Receptor Binding Detection Bead-Based Receptor Binding Detection\"\n- \"Human and NHP ortholog binding confirmed\"\n- \"Novel Receptors Highly Expressed in Neurons and Brain Endothelial Cells\"\n- \"NR004: endothelial-specific\", \"NR002: broad expression across CNS cell types, enabling intracellular delivery\"\n- \"Identified and patented novel human receptor with complete homology in NHPs and humans\"\n\nThese are excellent quotes. I'll verify via pdftotext locally to get exact strings.\n\nLet me now:\n1. mkdir the dir, curl Capsida PDF, pdftotext.\n2. Search GROMACS GPU benchmark + LRP6 AAV.\n3. Search AlphaFold-Multimer ipTM paper? Maybe not needed.\n\nAlso a docking benchmark source: \"ClusPro\" or \"LightDock\" — I'll cite LightDock paper for tool choice but not necessarily a runtime number (I'll measure in pilot / GUESS).\n\nAlso: is there an open page with Lambda pricing I should fetch to confirm? The prompt gives page_text; I'll cite https://lambda.ai/pricing with that text. Good enough (CITED).\n\nLet me proceed."
