ain and the full length extracellular domain of mouse LRP6 but not that of closely-related LRP5\"; \"AAV9, on the other hand, bound only to AAVR's PKD2\"\n- \"AAV9-X1.1, like PHP.eB, had a slightly reduced affinity for AAVR PKD2 compared to AAV9\"\n- \"SPR confirms that the engineered capsids AAV9-X1.1 and CAP-Mac gained direct binding interactions with human LRP6\"\n- Table 1 gives capsid sequences/variants (AAV9-X1.1, CAP-Mac, AAV-BI30, etc.) — perfect for the capsid panel with known bind/no-bind readouts!\n\nThis gives me a public proxy binding panel with real readouts:\n- AAV9: binds AAVR-PKD2 (yes), LRP6 (no), LY6A (no) [Huang 2019: Ly6a did not increase AAV9 binding]\n- AAV9-X1.1: LRP6 (yes), AAVR-PKD2 (yes, slightly reduced), galactose (yes)\n- CAP-Mac: LRP6 (yes), AAVR-PKD2 (yes, similar to AAV9)\n- AAV1-X1: LRP6 (yes); AAV1: LRP6 (no)\n- AAVDJ-X1: LRP6 (yes); AAV-DJ: LRP6 (no)\n- PHP.eB: LY6A (yes), AAVR-PKD2 (reduced vs AAV9)\n- AAV-BI30: LRP6-E1E2 (yes)\n- AAV2: AAVR-PKD2 (yes), HSPG (yes)\n- AAV5: AAVR-PKD1 (yes)\n- VCAP-102: ALPL (yes, KD ~20 nM), AAVR (required)\n- AAV9 vs ALPL: \"no difference was observed with the parental capsid, AAV9\" (ALPL paper) → AAV9: ALPL (no)\n\nThat's a rich reference panel of bind/no-bind with published geometry (AAV2-AAVR 3-fold axis; IL3 at 3-fold spike side; PHP.eB LY6A at VR-VIII 7-mer; LRP6 binds VR-VIII peptide; VCAP-102 peptide in ALPL catalytic pocket).\n\nNow the plan becomes concrete and checkable:\nBuild: a public-data pipeline that (1) builds capsid surface trimers (3-fold) for a panel of AAV capsids with known receptor readouts; (2) docks receptor ectodomains/peptides (ALPL, AAVR-PKD2, LRP6-E1E2, LY6A, plus negative partners LRP5, IL3); (3) runs AlphaFold-Multimer (ColabFold) with5 models × up to 20 recycles (matching Shay et al. config); (4) MD-refines top poses (GROMACS, 20–100 ns); (5) emits calls in plate/bead assay format (as Capsida's NR001-NR005 slide: plate-based and bead-based receptor binding detecti